nd $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/6c/6c0f164deb5815fc1c79e3dd724b6725168213938a81089867f4343cb4f05974.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/5d/5dc5186154c40546a088db1890991e83c6f594d0042866ae9b86cddb3f2d08d8.svg)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](images/fa/fad28fb44ef22f703cbc8bd6a07d7d35e4a77ffe4fb3cd0ec5fdd3b107317a1b.svg)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 7\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1=7a \\\\ b-3=7b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](images/29/29dcb07dde2cdecb330fddb6168319527336ed7a217506727aa6c28241e32a4c.svg)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](images/3e/3e1b5e881fb3c6d5688fd4978ed0fcc16aec5c6e105c11b919a6a9810762d698.svg)" 13194139535473 1